-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Design credit: yorukot/superfile — patterns only, NO CODE IS VENDORED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

lw's TUI takes design inspiration from yorukot/superfile
(https://github.com/yorukot/superfile), commit
b72f550bc6e75913f48eb49fdd258e1a2df2fe88, licensed MIT.

To state this plainly, because it matters: NO SOURCE CODE FROM SUPERFILE IS
COPIED, ADAPTED, OR VENDORED ANYWHERE IN THIS REPOSITORY. There is no
`third_party/` directory and no superfile package appears in go.mod. What
lw's own, independently written Go code borrows is three *patterns*:

  1. the three-pane sidebar / browser / preview panel layout
     (internal/ui and its screen sub-packages);
  2. a flat, superfile-style `key = value` theme.toml — adapted here with
     paired "<name>_light" / "<name>_dark" keys per colour, because
     lipgloss v2 resolves colour by calling a LightDarkFunc at style-build
     time (charm.land/lipgloss/v2's lipgloss.LightDark) rather than by
     shipping one theme file per background polarity the way superfile
     does;
  3. a flat `key_name = ["stroke", ...]` hotkeys.toml, mapping one named
     action to a list of keystrokes.

An earlier design (/.dev-notes/PLAN-v1.md D1) called for vendoring three of superfile's
Go packages (pkg/file_preview, pkg/string_function, pkg/utils) under
third_party/. That plan was measured against yorukot/superfile@b72f550
before any code was written and reversed: those three packages pull in
twelve modules outside this project's dependency allowlist — including
stretchr/testify, which the allowlist bans outright, and a second TOML
library where this project already standardises on BurntSushi/toml — for
functionality (an image thumbnailer; a lipgloss v1 Canvas/Layer workaround
that lipgloss v2 already ships natively) this project does not use. See
the build's MASTER §9 decision D-CK.

